insert into public.quiz_questions (id,quiz_id,question_text,question_type,options,correct_option,explanation,position,published) values
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','Which stage comes first in the AI Project Cycle?','multiple_choice','["Evaluation","Problem scoping","Modelling","Data exploration"]',1,'Problem scoping identifies the challenge before collecting or exploring data.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','A responsible AI system should consider who might be affected by its decisions.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',0,'Thinking about affected people and communities is part of responsible, human-centred AI.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','A school tool may unfairly exclude some students. What should the team do?','scenario','["Ignore it if most results look right","Review the data and outcomes for bias","Collect more personal data from everyone","Hide how recommendations are made"]',1,'Reviewing representation and outcomes can reveal unfair patterns so the system can be improved.',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','Which principle helps people understand why an AI system made a decision?','multiple_choice','["Transparency","Speed","Storage","Automation"]',0,'Transparency helps people understand and question a system’s decisions.',3,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002','In supervised learning, training examples include…','multiple_choice','["Labels or known answers","Only pictures","No examples","Random predictions"]',0,'Supervised learning learns from examples paired with labels or known outcomes.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002','Clustering can find groups in data without pre-labelled answers.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',0,'Clustering is an unsupervised approach for grouping similar examples.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002','A model does well on practice examples but poorly on new examples. What may be happening?','scenario','["It generalises perfectly","It may have overfit its training data","It always needs fewer examples","The labels are no longer needed"]',1,'Overfitting happens when a model learns training details that do not generalise to new data.',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002','What is one role of neural-network weights?','multiple_choice','["Store adjustable strengths of connections","Choose the school timetable","Create labels in every case","Replace all data"]',0,'Weights adjust connection strengths and are tuned as a network learns.',3,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003','Why keep test data separate from training data?','multiple_choice','["Estimate performance on unseen examples","Make training slower","Remove all errors","Label the model"]',0,'A separate test set gives a more honest estimate of performance on new data.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003','Accuracy alone is always the best metric for every problem.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',1,'The right metric depends on the problem; precision and recall may matter more in some cases.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003','A filter must avoid missing suspicious messages. Which metric should you focus on?','scenario','["Recall","Screen brightness","File size","Training time"]',0,'Recall measures how many actual positive cases the system catches.',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003','A confusion matrix compares…','multiple_choice','["Predicted and actual labels","Two training datasets","Only model speed","Images and sound"]',0,'A confusion matrix shows how predictions compare with actual classes.',3,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004','Which measure is often less affected by an extreme outlier?','multiple_choice','["Median","Mean","Range","Total"]',0,'The median is based on the middle value and is less influenced by extreme values than the mean.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004','A graph title and labelled axes help readers interpret data.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',0,'Titles and labels make chart quantities and context clear.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004','One unusually high value pulls the average up. Which summary might better show a typical value?','scenario','["Median","Maximum","Sum","Count"]',0,'The median is robust to an extreme value and can better describe the middle of the data.',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004','A data distribution describes…','multiple_choice','["How values are spread and occur","Only a chart colour","The model’s name","Predictions only"]',0,'A distribution describes the pattern, frequency and spread of values.',3,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000017','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005','A digital image is made up of small units called…','multiple_choice','["Pixels","Paragraphs","Labels","Functions"]',0,'Pixels are the small picture elements that make up a digital image.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000018','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005','Object detection can identify and locate objects in an image.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',0,'Object detection classifies objects and locates them, often with boxes.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005','A wildlife camera needs to count and locate animals in each photo. Which task fits?','scenario','["Object detection","Text translation","Sentence clustering","Audio transcription"]',0,'Object detection can find and locate multiple animals in a picture.',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005','Image classification usually assigns…','multiple_choice','["A label to an image","A sound to a video","A password to a camera","A chart to every pixel"]',0,'Image classification predicts a category or label for an image.',3,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006','NLP is a field of AI that works with…','multiple_choice','["Human language","Only gears","Network cables","Screen pixels only"]',0,'Natural Language Processing helps computers work with human language.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000022','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006','A chatbot can use intent detection to infer what a person wants to do.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',0,'Intent detection classifies the goal or request expressed in a message.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000023','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006','A shop wants to group reviews into positive and negative opinions. Which task fits?','scenario','["Sentiment analysis","Object detection","Image cropping","Sorting by file size"]',0,'Sentiment analysis estimates the opinion or emotional tone expressed in text.',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000024','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006','Breaking text into smaller units for processing is commonly called…','multiple_choice','["Tokenisation","Regression","Cropping","Encryption"]',0,'Tokenisation splits text into manageable units such as words or subwords.',3,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000025','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007','Why use a function in Python?','multiple_choice','["Organise reusable instructions","Make a screen larger","Delete every variable","Turn all data into a picture"]',0,'Functions group reusable instructions under a meaningful name.',0,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000026','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007','A Python dictionary stores values using key-value pairs.','true_or_false','["True","False"]',0,'Dictionaries associate keys with corresponding values.',1,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000027','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007','You need to keep each student’s name linked to a quiz score. Which structure fits?','scenario','["A dictionary","A comment","A Boolean value","A print statement"]',0,'A dictionary can map each student name (key) to a score (value).',2,true),
('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000028','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007','In a Python for loop, the indented block is…','multiple_choice','["Repeated for each item","Always skipped","An image type","A dictionary key"]',0,'A for loop runs its indented body for each item in a collection.',3,true)
